Does anyone here regard extropianism as an end in itself?  I doubt it.  It
is an approach to having fun in the universe.  I revere the marketplace
because it brings me good food and good toys.  I love technology for the
same reason.  Mathematics, logic and linguistics give me toys that I can
play with even when I'm sick in bed or stuck on a bus.

> 10.  There is a group called "Global Awareness Through Experience".  Their
> thesis is that symbols (such as writing, picutres, newscasts) don't
> actually convey the meaning of powerful concepts such as starvation,
> disease, hatred, war, etc.  This group takes people to visit places like
